$OpenBSD$

+-----------------------------------------------------------------------
| Running ${PKGSTEM} on OpenBSD
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------

This is an initial RPC-client port, not an operational OpenBSD VPN client.
Most commands require a compatible mullvad-daemon through its Unix socket,
/var/run/mullvad-vpn. MULLVAD_RPC_SOCKET_PATH can override the socket path;
the upstream CLI does not connect directly to a remote TCP daemon.

The daemon subpackage is intentionally disabled and BROKEN. The native
backend groundwork must not be interpreted as implemented leak protection.
No daemon, rc service, PF anchor or resolver change is installed by this
CLI package. Do not use it as evidence that your traffic is protected.

The prospective daemon socket defaults to root-only mode 0600 on OpenBSD.
Upstream's MULLVAD_MANAGEMENT_SOCKET_GROUP can grant a chosen group access;
membership allows privileged VPN/account control, not merely status queries.
There is no new RPC protocol or world-writable socket fallback on OpenBSD.
